// custom_models/night_train.json
// Shared base model for every night_train* profile. Track GAUGE is not
// decided here — each profile adds exactly one nt_gauge_<mm>.json alongside
// this file (see config.yml). Rules are independent `if` clauses rather
// than an else_if chain, because GraphHopper concatenates the rule lists of
// all custom_model_files and a chain cannot span files; multiply_by 0 is
// absorbing, so the two forms are equivalent anyway.
//
// The 230 limit is a GRAPH-LEVEL ceiling, not a per-trip speed: it bounds
// the paths that send no composition (route_geometry, and simpleRouting
// until G3). fullRouting caps every trip at its own
// composition.max_speed_kmh in the request custom model, which is always
// <= 230, so this never binds there. Sanctioned mirror of
// MAX_COMPOSITION_SPEED_KMH in models/route/model.py — keep the two equal.
//
// Belarus and Russia are excluded from routing by project decision, but NOT
// here: GraphHopper's `country` encoded value is unavailable in this fork,
// so the block is applied per request as an area rule in
// rail_router._build_custom_model(), the same way HSR avoidance is.
//
// Power systems: 25kV 50Hz AC, 15kV 16.7Hz AC, 3kV DC, 1.5kV DC + diesel.
// Use with: [rail.json, nt_gauge_<mm>.json, preferred_direction.json]

{
  "distance_influence": 0.2,
  "speed": [
    { "if": "railway_service == YARD || railway_service == SPUR",
      "multiply_by": "0" },
    { "if": "true",
      "limit_to": "230" }
  ]
}
